      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IDEN OLIVER (2) won two back at Launceston from a nice gate. Drew wide last start and was easily accounted for, beaten 22 metres into fourth at this track over 2090m. No excuses from this more advantageous draw. Finds a nice race and can make amends. KNOCK OUT NZ (1) was out of the money two runs ago then broke and finished sixth last start over 2090m here, coming home 12 metres from the winner. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Big chance if he behaves in this similar assignment. DONNY IN PARIS (8) is the next best after finishing third over 2090m at this circuit last time out. Top-three aspirations. CAN FEEL THE FURY NZ (5) disappointed last time but is a hope based on a solid second over 1680m at Launceston two runs back. Worth another chance.",
